1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:05,900
And that concludes the life of Adam Smith,
the founder of economics.

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:12,110
While you're taking notes, let's discuss
the reports you submitted last time.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:16,510
Regarding how resources and services
are distributed in Canada and Japan.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,760
Since he left for Canada,
two and a half years have flown by.

5
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,870
I'm already a sophomore in college.

6
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,350
I was busy with college entrance exams.

7
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:30,960
And he was busy adjusting to his new life.

8
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:35,670
In the end, I never made it to Canada.

9
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:38,950
We only saw each other once
when he visited Japan.

10
00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:44,000
Even though we kept in touch,

11
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:48,064
sometimes I can't help but wonder
if that summer was just a dream.

12
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,059
Has anyone read it?

13
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,340
Take a look.

14
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:57,880
It's available in bookstores
and online.

15
00:00:57,904 --> 00:01:00,004
(Incoming Call: Saeki)

16
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,959
Huh?

17
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,040
You're still awake?

18
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:15,060
I was watching a movie.

19
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:20,020
Yeah, that'll definitely keep you up.

20
00:01:21,070 --> 00:01:22,070
Yeah.

21
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:24,370
Okay.

22
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,400
See you later, then.

23
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:29,920
Ah, wait.

24
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:32,690
I forgot to tell you.

25
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:38,420
Welcome back,

26
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:40,470
Saeki.

27
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:47,500
I'm back, Wataru.

28
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:28,440
Our relationship has been stuck
in that summer.

29
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,820
But if we can be by
each other's side again...

30
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:13,400
"My Summer Of You"
(Episode 7)

31
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,650
Hey.

32
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:39,419
Wataru, you got here fast.

33
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:42,090
Yeah, my second class was canceled.

34
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:47,300
It's been so long since I saw you.

35
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:50,280
Wait, I can't breathe!

36
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,550
Sorry, sorry.

37
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:54,330
It's fine.

38
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,160
You just got back.

39
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:58,159
Sorry, was I too eager?

40
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,880
No, I'm really happy.

41
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,700
Come on in.

42
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:03,060
Okay.

43
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,430
Excuse me.

44
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:09,509
Make yourself at home.

45
00:05:09,510 --> 00:05:10,310
Okay.

46
00:05:10,311 --> 00:05:11,899
Is soda okay?

47
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:13,100
Yeah, thanks.

48
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,079
Did your mom prepare all this?

49
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,080
Yeah.

50
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,400
She came back early to set it up for me.

51
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:23,380
That's so sweet of her.

52
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:27,616
By the way, you were interning at that film
company until the very last minute, right?

53
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:28,699
That's amazing.

54
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,090
It's no big deal.

55
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:32,999
I just happened to have some free
time after graduating high school.

56
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,910
I see.

57
00:05:33,950 --> 00:05:34,950
Here you go.

58
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:38,290
I bought this because I wanted
to drink it with you.

59
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,090
Thanks.

60
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:47,119
By the way, you could've gone to college
over there, but you came back here.

61
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,259
Are you sure about that?

62
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,260
Of course.

63
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:52,850
I always planned to take a gap year
and go to college here.

64
00:05:53,840 --> 00:05:54,840
Besides,

65
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:59,000
I want to hurry up and continue
the story from that summer.

66
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:02,359
Are you okay?

67
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,360
I'm fine.

68
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:05,020
The soda just went down the wrong pipe.

69
00:06:14,190 --> 00:06:14,790
Ah.

70
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:17,150
I should probably head to work.

71
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,499
Huh? You just got here.

72
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,340
Sorry.

73
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:21,520
I forgot they asked me to come in early.

74
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:24,769
Huh? I'll walk you down, then.

75
00:06:24,770 --> 00:06:27,300
No need, it's really fine.

76
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:29,330
Thanks for the Ramune.

77
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:31,720
I'll text you later.

78
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:32,970
Okay.

79
00:06:43,320 --> 00:06:47,240
We finally get to see each other,
and what the hell am I doing?

80
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:50,420
He's gotten so much more mature.

81
00:06:50,570 --> 00:06:52,620
And he smells really good, too.

82
00:06:57,910 --> 00:07:00,520
What did he mean by continuing
the story from that summer?

83
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:04,980
We got separated right after
I realized I liked him.

84
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:09,010
Even if he says he wants to continue it...

85
00:07:15,050 --> 00:07:17,270
This is so embarrassing.

86
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:19,430
What's so embarrassing?

87
00:07:19,430 --> 00:07:20,430
Huh?

88
00:07:20,930 --> 00:07:22,130
Nothing, it's nothing.

89
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,290
Toda, aren't you here a bit too early?

90
00:07:24,490 --> 00:07:26,690
Ah, my classes ended early.

91
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:27,780
So I came to help out.

92
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:28,530
Thanks.

93
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:30,810
Then could you help Niimi
clean up the seating area?

94
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:32,420
I'll add some extra hours to your shift.

95
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:33,480
Thanks, Manager.

96
00:07:37,230 --> 00:07:39,550
Is it going to be busy today, too?

97
00:07:40,030 --> 00:07:42,350
It should be better than the weekend.

98
00:07:44,390 --> 00:07:45,630
Oh, right.

99
00:07:46,290 --> 00:07:49,209
Zaizen's "Blueprint" is
coming out soon, right?

100
00:07:49,210 --> 00:07:51,589
Toda, that's your
favorite director, isn't it?

101
00:07:51,590 --> 00:07:52,430
Yeah.

102
00:07:52,590 --> 00:07:56,410
In high school, my friend and I even
went on a pilgrimage for "Sea of Light."

103
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:58,870
Next Saturday,

104
00:07:59,550 --> 00:08:01,329
we're having an advance screening here.

105
00:08:01,330 --> 00:08:02,730
Seriously?

106
00:08:03,450 --> 00:08:05,870
The theater manager gave me two tickets.

107
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:08,790
If you're free, want to watch it together?

108
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:10,390
Huh?

109
00:08:10,850 --> 00:08:11,850
Ah.

110
00:08:11,870 --> 00:08:13,360
Do you already have plans?

111
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:15,710
No.

112
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:19,110
Even though I don't have plans yet,

113
00:08:20,410 --> 00:08:23,290
it should be fine if I go
with someone else, right?

114
00:08:24,890 --> 00:08:26,090
No, I don't have plans.

115
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:27,110
I'd love to go.

116
00:08:28,290 --> 00:08:29,290
Okay.

117
00:08:29,410 --> 00:08:32,089
We can figure out the details later.

118
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,150
Sounds good.

119
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:38,140
I can always just ask him
to go together next time.

120
00:08:53,378 --> 00:08:55,465
Can we meet tomorrow?

121
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,899
(Wataru: Can we meet tomorrow? I have something to
tell you.) (Chiharu: Of course. When and where?)

122
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,553
(Wataru: I'll be at your uni at 12:30. Wait at
the stairs by the main gate.) (Chiharu: Got it.)

123
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:15,930
Hey.

124
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,550
Wataru.

125
00:09:17,610 --> 00:09:18,866
Sorry for asking you out so suddenly.

126
00:09:18,890 --> 00:09:20,719
I should be the one apologizing
for making you come all the way here.

127
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,369
It's no problem at all.

128
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:24,309
I don't have work today,
so I'm completely free.

129
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:25,850
Should we head to the cafeteria, then?

130
00:09:25,890 --> 00:09:27,126
I heard the food is really good.

131
00:09:27,150 --> 00:09:28,110
Sounds great.

132
00:09:28,111 --> 00:09:29,429
- Alright, let's go.
- This way.

133
00:09:29,430 --> 00:09:30,430
Okay.

134
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:34,149
What should we get?

135
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:35,150
Ah.

136
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:36,926
You said you had something to tell me.

137
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:37,980
Chiharu!

138
00:09:39,490 --> 00:09:40,780
Akiyoshi.

139
00:09:41,410 --> 00:09:42,950
I finally found you.

140
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:44,450
When did you get back?

141
00:09:44,830 --> 00:09:45,969
You could've at least texted me.

142
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:48,790
Sorry, I just got back yesterday.
Today's my first day on campus.

143
00:09:48,950 --> 00:09:49,950
I see.

144
00:09:51,610 --> 00:09:52,910
- A friend of yours?
- Yeah.

145
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:55,389
A friend from high school. He
came all the way here to hang out.

146
00:09:55,390 --> 00:09:57,529
Is this the legendary movie buff?

147
00:09:57,530 --> 00:09:58,530
Yeah.

148
00:09:58,590 --> 00:09:59,300
I see.

149
00:09:59,301 --> 00:10:01,360
We're heading to the cafeteria.
Wanna join us?

150
00:10:01,890 --> 00:10:03,110
Yeah, I'd love to.

151
00:10:03,890 --> 00:10:04,810
Let's all go together, then.

152
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:05,810
Okay.

153
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:08,600
Ah, I'm starving.

154
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:11,220
Let's dig in.

155
00:10:13,430 --> 00:10:16,949
Oh, so you two went to the
same high school in Canada.

156
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:17,950
Yeah.

157
00:10:18,170 --> 00:10:20,570
And you both got into the
same university's Faculty of Arts.

158
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:23,830
I want to be a film director,
so I'm majoring in film.

159
00:10:24,370 --> 00:10:27,349
Chiharu wants to be a film
translator, so he's majoring in English.

160
00:10:27,350 --> 00:10:28,220
That's right.

161
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:29,290
Huh?

162
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:32,080
Hmm?

163
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:33,409
You didn't tell him?

164
00:10:33,410 --> 00:10:34,410
Ah.

165
00:10:35,090 --> 00:10:37,320
I was planning to tell
Wataru after I got here.

166
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:39,760
It's fine.

167
00:10:40,450 --> 00:10:42,820
I see. So that's why
you're majoring in English.

168
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,140
Yeah.

169
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:52,110
Daniel just texted me.

170
00:10:52,450 --> 00:10:53,610
Did you get one too, Chiharu?

171
00:10:53,830 --> 00:10:54,480
Yeah, I did.

172
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:54,830
You did?

173
00:10:54,831 --> 00:10:56,391
The message is almost exactly the same.

174
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,820
I knew it.

175
00:10:59,430 --> 00:11:00,450
That's so like Daniel.

176
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:01,490
Hilarious, right?

177
00:11:04,310 --> 00:11:06,220
So, what about you, Toda-kun?

178
00:11:06,430 --> 00:11:07,589
Are you also looking
to get into filmmaking?

179
00:11:07,590 --> 00:11:08,590
Huh?

180
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:10,670
Ah, aren't you into movies?

181
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:17,190
Right now, I'm just
focused on watching them.

182
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:19,340
And I'm majoring in economics.

183
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:22,140
I see.

184
00:11:25,590 --> 00:11:26,790
Oh, right.

185
00:11:26,850 --> 00:11:29,350
Someone from my department
just gave me two movie tickets.

186
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:31,529
For Director Zaizen's "Blueprint."

187
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:32,559
Oh, really?

188
00:11:32,560 --> 00:11:33,580
Wanna go together?

189
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:38,110
Hmm.

190
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,120
Ah, do you want to come
along too, Toda-kun?

191
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,320
Ah.

192
00:11:42,570 --> 00:11:43,710
About that movie,

193
00:11:43,830 --> 00:11:46,680
the theater where I work is
hosting an advance screening.

194
00:11:46,950 --> 00:11:48,750
Oh, they have events like that?

195
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,350
Does that mean

196
00:11:50,850 --> 00:11:52,280
you get to see it early, Toda-kun?

197
00:11:52,430 --> 00:11:54,249
I guess so.

198
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:55,960
Wow, you're so lucky.

199
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:59,250
So, when are you free?

200
00:11:59,830 --> 00:12:02,819
I'm not sure about my class schedule yet.
Can I let you know later?

201
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:03,820
Okay.

202
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:16,916
With Akiyoshi around, life in
Canada must have been pretty fun.

203
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:17,950
Yeah.

204
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:19,550
He helped me out a lot in so many ways.

205
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,070
I see.

206
00:12:21,810 --> 00:12:23,860
Oh, didn't you have something to say?

207
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:27,469
Not really. We just didn't get a
chance to talk much yesterday.

208
00:12:27,470 --> 00:12:28,670
Oh, right.

209
00:12:30,350 --> 00:12:33,600
Um, do you want to come over to
my place next week or the week after?

210
00:12:33,870 --> 00:12:35,016
I finally got my internet set up.

211
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,600
I thought maybe we could watch a movie.

212
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:39,030
Oh, sure.

213
00:12:39,370 --> 00:12:40,749
Let me check my work schedule.

214
00:12:40,750 --> 00:12:41,750
Okay.

215
00:12:41,810 --> 00:12:42,850
I'm looking forward to it.

216
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,180
I should get going.

217
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:47,449
But there's still some time before class.

218
00:12:47,450 --> 00:12:51,280
I can't. I forgot about an assignment,
and the deadline is coming up.

219
00:12:52,270 --> 00:12:53,060
See ya.

220
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:54,060
Yeah.

221
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:08,470
Guchi: It's been a while. Want to hang out?

222
00:13:15,870 --> 00:13:19,690
We just planned this yesterday and
everyone made it. We're awesome.

223
00:13:21,530 --> 00:13:22,530
By the way,

224
00:13:22,850 --> 00:13:24,090
why is Asada here?

225
00:13:24,490 --> 00:13:25,490
What's your problem?

226
00:13:25,550 --> 00:13:27,589
I heard we were having a rare get-together,
so I did you a favor by showing up.

227
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:29,990
Sorry.
I accidentally let it slip.

228
00:13:30,470 --> 00:13:32,490
You guys go to the same college, after all.

229
00:13:33,230 --> 00:13:35,786
If you were coming, you should've
brought some other girls along.

230
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:37,400
Classic Guchi.

231
00:13:37,550 --> 00:13:39,369
I didn't even think of that.

232
00:13:39,370 --> 00:13:40,670
That's nothing to be proud of.

233
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:43,269
This gratin brings back memories.

234
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:44,320
It really does.

235
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:45,780
Come to think of it,

236
00:13:46,150 --> 00:13:48,230
we used to hang out like
this in high school, right?

237
00:13:48,850 --> 00:13:50,280
Yeah, we totally did.

238
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,766
It feels just like when the four of us
used to hang out together.

239
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:55,689
Speaking of which,
is Saeki still in Canada?

240
00:13:55,690 --> 00:13:57,920
Toda, you've been keeping
in touch with him, right?

241
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:05,010
Sorry.

242
00:14:05,270 --> 00:14:07,090
I haven't told you guys.

243
00:14:07,840 --> 00:14:08,900
Actually...

244
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:12,810
Huh?

245
00:14:16,770 --> 00:14:18,450
You're saying he's in Japan?

246
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,230
Yeah, sorry.

247
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:21,609
Seriously?

248
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:24,290
Wait, so have you already seen Saeki, Toda?

249
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:25,820
Kind of...

250
00:14:26,170 --> 00:14:29,309
Hey, how has Saeki changed
since coming back from Canada?

251
00:14:29,310 --> 00:14:30,590
Is he still as handsome as ever?

252
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:32,009
You're asking me...?

253
00:14:34,330 --> 00:14:38,040
I guess he just seems
a bit more mature now.

254
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,509
Oh, I see.

255
00:14:40,510 --> 00:14:41,510
Still,

256
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:45,550
I haven't forgiven that guy
for transferring without saying a word.

257
00:14:48,970 --> 00:14:50,940
Let it go already.

258
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:53,230
Wataru already punched
him hard for it anyway.

259
00:14:53,310 --> 00:14:54,310
Right?

260
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:03,360
Yeah...

261
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:08,819
Whatever. If you're keeping in
touch with him because you want to,

262
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:09,860
then I have no objections.

263
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:14,046
But if you have something on your mind,
you need to speak up.

264
00:15:14,070 --> 00:15:16,950
I don't want to see you
make that kind of face again.

265
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:20,790
Guchi...

266
00:15:23,010 --> 00:15:25,520
Oh, but pass a message to Saeki for me.

267
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,880
What is it?

268
00:15:28,170 --> 00:15:29,860
If he ever pulls a stunt like that again,

269
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:32,520
I'll absolutely beat the crap out of him.

270
00:15:34,990 --> 00:15:36,820
- Hiraoka will beat him up.
- Why me?

271
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:38,610
Why do I have to do it?

272
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,139
I'll punch a hole right through him.

273
00:15:40,140 --> 00:15:41,110
What do you mean, punch a hole?

274
00:15:41,111 --> 00:15:42,229
I'll punch a hole right through him.

275
00:15:42,230 --> 00:15:43,489
- With your fist?
- With my fist.

276
00:15:43,490 --> 00:15:44,350
What the heck?

277
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:45,350
You think so too?

278
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:46,909
He even broke a wall before.

279
00:15:46,910 --> 00:15:48,129
I did not break a wall.

280
00:15:48,130 --> 00:15:49,849
- Why?
- You totally punched a hole in it.

281
00:15:49,850 --> 00:15:51,149
Your fists are the strongest, after all.

282
00:15:51,150 --> 00:15:53,029
Yeah, I'm the powerhouse type.

283
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:54,170
It's ridiculous.

284
00:15:54,410 --> 00:15:55,410
The power of those fists.

285
00:16:19,650 --> 00:16:20,650
Wataru?

286
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,100
Hey.

287
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:23,480
Is now a good time?

288
00:16:24,690 --> 00:16:25,540
Yeah.

289
00:16:25,710 --> 00:16:26,710
What's up?

290
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:30,210
Well,

291
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:37,680
a senior at work gave me tickets
to the advance screening of "Blueprint."

292
00:16:39,650 --> 00:16:41,010
Do you want to go see it together?

293
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,500
Huh?

294
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,000
If you're free, want to go together?

295
00:16:48,170 --> 00:16:49,210
I want to go.

296
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,300
Okay.

297
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:53,050
I'll give you the details later.

298
00:16:53,130 --> 00:16:54,220
Sounds good.

299
00:17:12,230 --> 00:17:13,360
Um, Niimi-san.

300
00:17:13,990 --> 00:17:14,990
Yeah?

301
00:17:15,350 --> 00:17:17,760
About the advance screening earlier,

302
00:17:18,950 --> 00:17:20,970
could you ask someone else to go with you?

303
00:17:22,670 --> 00:17:25,250
I don't mind.

304
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:26,910
Why the sudden change of heart?

305
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:28,340
Ah, well...

306
00:17:31,090 --> 00:17:33,450
There's someone I want to
watch it with for the first time.

307
00:17:34,110 --> 00:17:36,550
Oh, I see.

308
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,140
What's wrong?

309
00:17:38,970 --> 00:17:41,990
Then I'll give you the tickets,
and you can invite that person.

310
00:17:42,380 --> 00:17:43,380
Huh?

311
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:47,190
Are you sure?

312
00:17:51,670 --> 00:17:52,670
Ah... No, wait.

313
00:17:52,690 --> 00:17:54,210
Akiyoshi was the one who invited you.

314
00:17:54,250 --> 00:17:55,250
Sorry.

315
00:17:59,250 --> 00:18:00,250
No, it's not that.

316
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:01,590
I was just so happy.

317
00:18:04,790 --> 00:18:06,930
Let's go to the advance screening together.

318
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,460
Huh?

319
00:18:13,310 --> 00:18:14,310
Are you really sure?

320
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:16,670
Yeah.

321
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:19,300
I already turned Akiyoshi down.

322
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,680
What?

323
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,460
Because I want to watch it with you
for the first time, Wataru.

324
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:28,270
So, thank you.

325
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:36,240
Yeah, thank you.

326
00:18:58,000 --> 00:18:59,100
("Blueprint")

327
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:01,740
Am I finally starting to hallucinate?

328
00:19:02,050 --> 00:19:04,810
People are creatures who only see
what they want to see, after all.

329
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:06,890
I wish you had told me.

330
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,480
About your illness.

331
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:12,119
It's that cliché thing.
"I only wanted you to see me healthy."

332
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,860
That's way too selfish of you.

333
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:17,820
Keep filming.

334
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,510
That way,
we'll meet again someday.

335
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:26,680
Thank you.

336
00:19:27,620 --> 00:19:28,930
Thank you for saving me.

337
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:31,250
The feeling is mutual.

338
00:19:33,620 --> 00:19:37,920
Make sure you enjoy your life.

339
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:54,980
I literally burst into tears.

340
00:20:06,420 --> 00:20:08,759
Zaizen really is amazing.

341
00:20:08,782 --> 00:20:10,523
Yeah, he is.

342
00:20:10,790 --> 00:20:12,170
That's great to hear.

343
00:20:12,180 --> 00:20:13,460
Ah, Niimi-san.

344
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:17,019
Huh? Are you scheduled to work today?

345
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:19,039
Yeah, we ended up being short-staffed.

346
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:20,050
Toda?

347
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,399
Is this your friend?

348
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:23,400
Yeah.

349
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,349
He's my high school classmate.

350
00:20:25,350 --> 00:20:27,219
Oh, really? Were you in the same class?

351
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,060
All right, Saito-san.

352
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,060
Back to work.

353
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:30,180
Time to head back.

354
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:34,100
Well then, enjoy the rest
of your time with your friend.

355
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:35,460
Excuse us.

356
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:37,046
I'll get going then. Good work today.

357
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,070
Good work.

358
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:40,150
Good work.

359
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,800
Wataru, the person who
gave you the tickets was...

360
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:47,320
Yeah, that was Niimi-san.

361
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:49,370
Let's go.

362
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:50,580
Okay.

363
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,830
Wow, it's been a while since we came here.

364
00:20:56,750 --> 00:20:58,750
Let's sit for a bit.

365
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:00,050
Sure.

366
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,549
Coming here makes me feel a little nervous.

367
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:08,459
Huh? You get nervous over memories?

368
00:21:08,460 --> 00:21:09,930
Of course I do.

369
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:22,900
What's wrong?

370
00:21:26,100 --> 00:21:28,119
Ouch. What?

371
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,760
Hold on.
Wataru, what are you doing?

372
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,790
You're really here.

373
00:21:32,830 --> 00:21:33,830
Huh?

374
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:36,430
It finally feels like you're back.

375
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:40,839
Seeing you again after so long,

376
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:43,840
you seemed more mature,
and I felt a bit left behind.

377
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:51,009
But being able to watch
a movie and talk like this,

378
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,220
I'm really happy after all.

379
00:21:53,850 --> 00:21:55,940
I want to spend a little
more time with you.

380
00:22:00,300 --> 00:22:01,300
Thank goodness.

381
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,480
So I'm not the only one
who wants us to be together.

382
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:09,030
You seemed down the last time we met,
and it's been bothering me.

383
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:14,500
My feelings haven't changed since then.

384
00:22:17,330 --> 00:22:19,730
But if there's something on your mind,
I want you to tell me.

385
00:22:25,120 --> 00:22:26,120
Well,

386
00:22:28,540 --> 00:22:29,540
Yeah?

387
00:22:30,490 --> 00:22:32,100
Never mind. It's nothing.

388
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,599
Now I'm curious.

389
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:35,890
I said it's nothing.

390
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:38,190
Forget it then.

391
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:44,720
Chiharu...

392
00:22:48,480 --> 00:22:49,480
Huh?

393
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:51,740
I thought I just heard you call my name.

394
00:22:53,490 --> 00:22:56,040
Because Akiyoshi calls you Chiharu...

395
00:22:59,540 --> 00:23:02,440
Wait, were you feeling
down back then because...

396
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:03,960
Chiharu.

397
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:06,479
I finally get to see you.

398
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:07,880
When did you get back?

399
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:09,969
Daniel sent me a message.

400
00:23:09,970 --> 00:23:11,139
Did you get it too, Chiharu?

401
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:11,720
I did.

402
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:12,210
You did?

403
00:23:12,211 --> 00:23:13,811
The message was almost exactly the same.

404
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:19,649
I haven't even called you that yet,
and someone else beat me to it.

405
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:20,770
It's pretty frustrating.

406
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:33,080
Don't look at me like that.

407
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:36,430
Wataru, look at me.

408
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:46,569
(Next Episode Preview)
Chiharu.

409
00:24:46,570 --> 00:24:47,999
Wataru's birthday.

410
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Salmon, right?
And tuna mayo.

411
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,319
Can I kiss you?

412
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:54,859
If I were stuck in bed with a fever,
how would you feel?

413
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:56,279
I'd want to take care of you.

414
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:59,080
I want to step up at a time like this too.

